@prefix actuation: <http://example.org/orexis/actuation#> .
@prefix execution: <http://example.org/orexis/execution#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix sensing: <http://example.org/orexis/sensing#> .
@prefix sosa: <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<> a orexis:OntologyGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  OREXIS ACTUATION: the translation row's acting side, the mirror of sensing - a step's command turned into what a
#  device is told and sent through the transport, in SOSA's words for acting (sosa:Actuator, sosa:Actuation,
#  sosa:actsOnProperty), declaring only what SOSA lacks
#  (knowledge/decisions/the-transport-is-the-bottom-layer-and-the-row-above-owns-the-loop.md). The words of a domain
#  that doses or heats - a valve, how fast it pours - are that domain's, in domains/actuation/.

#  THE ROLE THIS PACKAGE SERVES (knowledge/domain/actuation/operator.md).
actuation:Operator a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf orexis:Role ; rdfs:label "Operator" ;
    rdfs:comment "An agent that operates devices: what a step it takes commands, and a board whose reading sensing says is due, is told through the transport, by the actuation package this role loads. It depends on no role: it acts on what an executor commands where one is played, and on what an observer says due where one is." .

#  WHAT AN AGENT OPERATES, and what a device changes.
actuation:hasActuator a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain orexis:Agent ; rdfs:range sosa:Actuator ;
    rdfs:label "has actuator" ;
    rdfs:comment "A device an agent may take a step through. The dose is available only on an actuator the agent holds." .
actuation:actuates a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sosa:Actuator ; rdfs:label "actuates" ;
    rdfs:comment "The subject the device changes: the bed a pump waters." .
actuation:actuatesProperty a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain sosa:Actuator ; rdfs:range sosa:ObservableProperty ;
    rdfs:label "actuates property" ;
    rdfs:comment "Which of the subject's properties the device moves: the soil's moisture for a pump. What the subject is believed of that property is what a dose changes, and a reading of it is what answers the dose." .

#  WHAT THE OPERATOR DOES, and what starts it: a step's commands, execution's , beneath its trigger.
actuation:Trigger a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf orexis:Event ; rdfs:label "Trigger" ;
    rdfs:comment "An event that starts an activity of the operator's." .

actuation:Actuating a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf prov:Activity ; rdfs:label "Actuating" ;
    rdfs:comment "One order of a step's commands sent: each actuator the command graph sets sent one document, every value written at its property's `actuation:commandPointer`, through the transport member that reaches it, and what was sent kept as an `actuation:ActuationGraph`; a setting with no pointer, and an actuator no member reaches, passed over, said in the log." .

actuation:ActuatingTrigger a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf actuation:Trigger ; rdfs:label "Actuating trigger" ;
    rdfs:comment "What starts an actuating: execution's `execution:Commanded`, beneath it here, naming the command graph a step's order kept (`execution:commands`)." .

execution:Commanded rdfs:subClassOf actuation:ActuatingTrigger .

actuation:Nudging a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf prov:Activity ; rdfs:label "Nudging" ;
    rdfs:comment "The boards of sensors whose readings are due told to sense: each sensor sent `actuation:SenseNow` set true, at its pointer, through the transport member that reaches it, not kept, since a nudge is no step's act; one no member reaches passed over, said in the log." .

actuation:NudgingTrigger a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf actuation:Trigger ; rdfs:label "Nudging trigger" ;
    rdfs:comment "What starts a nudging: sensing's `sensing:ReadingLapsed`, beneath it here, naming each sensor due (`sensing:lapsed`)." .

sensing:ReadingLapsed rdfs:subClassOf actuation:NudgingTrigger .

actuation:SenseNow a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf sosa:ActuatableProperty ; rdfs:label "Sense now" ;
    actuation:commandPointer "/sense" ;
    rdfs:comment "Whether a board reads its sensors now: what a nudge sets true, sent as `sense`, so a board that wakes on its own time reports at once." .

#  WHAT A DEVICE IS SENT, the mirror of what sensing reads: a property says where in the document its value is written,
#  as a sensor says where in the document its reading is (`sensing:readingPointer`).
actuation:commandPointer a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:string ; rdfs:label "command pointer" ;
    rdfs:comment "Where in the JSON document a device is sent a value of this `sosa:ActuatableProperty` is written: an RFC 6901 pointer, `/dose_ml` for a dose's volume, `/to/x` for a van's column. Stated by the domain that declares the property, as its command's text once wrote the key itself; every value one order sets on one actuator goes into one document." .

#  WHAT THE OPERATOR KEEPS of what it sent.
actuation:ActuationGraph a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf orexis:Graph ; rdfs:label "Actuation graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "The acts one actuating made, kept as the agent's own (`orexis:Recorded`): a `sosa:Actuation` per setting sent, the actuator that made it (`sosa:madeByActuator`), the property it acted on (`sosa:actsOnProperty`), the value (`sosa:hasSimpleResult`) and the instant it was sent (`sosa:resultTime`). What a command graph asked and no member reached is in none. No belief, and handed to no reader of the mind." .
